===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|なまくら|alt=鈍ら}}

The first portion ''nama'' is from {{m|ja|生|tr=nama}}.  This usually has a sense of {{m|en|raw}} but also has overtones of {{m|en|[[unprocessed]], [[unready]]}} and thus some semantic overlap with, and is cognate with, {{m|ja|鈍る|tr=namaru||to become [[dull]], especially due to lack of proper [[tempering]]}}.

The second portion ''kura'' is of uncertain derivation.

The term is first cited to 1711.<ref name="KDJ"/>

