===Etymology 2===
{{zh-forms|s=钿|alt=錢}}
Most likely a variant reading of {{zh-l|錢|tr=-}} that underwent further semantic development in Wu. The use of this exact glyph in place of {{zh-l|錢|tr=-}} is more commonly found in Northern Wu.

The exact route through which this morpheme came to have a {{IPAchar|/d/}} initial is disputed, argued either to be a substrate retention or through initial assimilation within the word {{zh-l|銅鈿|tr=-}}. Compare for instance Suzhounese {{zh-l|錢|surname|tr=<sup>2</sup>zie}} and {{zh-l|鈿|money (chiefly in compounds)|tr=<sup>2</sup>die}}; as opposed to Jinhuanese {{zh-l|錢|surname|tr=<sup>2</sup>die}} and {{zh-l|鈿|money (chiefly in compounds)|tr=<sup>2</sup>die}}. Also confer Wuxinese {{zh-l|銅錢|money; metal coin|tr=-}} {{IPAchar|/doŋ ziɪ/}} or Danyangnese {{zh-l|銅錢|money; metal coin|tr=-}} {{IPAchar|/tɔŋ tɕɪ/}}.

