===Etymology 1===
<div style="float:right;">
{{wp|ja:はさみ}}
[[File:Small_Scissors.jpg|thumb|250px|{{lang|ja|鋏}} (''hasami''): a pair of traditional Japanese '''shears''' or '''scissors'''.]]
[[File:Pair of scissors with black handle.jpg|thumb|250px|{{lang|ja|鋏}} (''hasami''): a pair of western-style '''scissors'''.]]
{{wp|Scissors}}
</div>
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|はさみ|alt=ハサミ,剪刀,螯,鉗}}
Originally the {{m|ja|連用形|tr=ren'yōkei||stem or continuative form}} of verb {{m|ja|鋏む|tr=hasamu||to be tightly between two things, to be inserted in between”}},<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref name="DJR">{{R:Daijirin}}</ref> itself apparently deriving from ''hasa'' (“narrowness between other things”, likely cognate with {{m|ja|細|tr=hoso}}, “skinny, narrowness within the thing itself”) + auxiliary suffix {{m|ja|む|tr=mu||to be or become like something}}.

Cognate and homophonic with {{m|ja|挟}}, {{m|ja|挿|tr=hasami}}: “being stuck in between other things”.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ja-pron|はさみ|acc=3|acc2=2|acc_ref=DJR,SMK5|acc2_ref=DJR,SMK5}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|はさみ}}

# a {{gl|[[pair]] of}} [[scissors]]
# {{ja-def|螯|ハサミ}} {{lb|ja|zootomy|sort=はさみ}} [[pincers]], [[claw]]s, or [[chela]] as found on a [[crab]], [[lobster]], or other [[arthropod]]
# a [[punch]] as used to make a [[hole]] in a [[piece]] of [[paper]]

=====Usage notes=====
The ''scissors'' and ''punch'' senses are also found spelled {{ja-l|剪刀}}.

The ''arthropod pincers'' sense is also found spelled {{ja-l|螯}} and {{ja-l|鉗}}.

=====Idioms=====
* {{ja-r|鋏を入れる|はさみ を いれる|to put the scissors in → to cut with scissors; to punch a ticket; to trim vegetation or hair}}

